          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्टैंड — sṭaiṇḍ — \"a stand (for buses, taxis or rickshaws)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बस स्टैंड यहाँ से पास है। bas sṭaiṇḍ yahā̃ se pās hai. The bus stand is close to here."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्टैंड (sṭaiṇḍ) is borrowed from English stand, the place where buses, taxis or rickshaws wait for passengers: बस स्टैंड, रिक्शा स्टैंड."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
